name: sim.setObjectParent
description: Sets an object's parent object. Dynamically simulated objects, together with their hierarchy tree, are dynamically reset (this however does not apply to static shapes)
luaSynopsis: sim.setObjectParent(int objectHandle, int parentObjectHandle, bool keepInPlace)
pythonSynopsis: sim.setObjectParent(int objectHandle, int parentObjectHandle, bool keepInPlace)
inputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the object that will become child of the parent object. Can be or-combined with sim.handleflag_assembly if an assembly operation is desired instead (in that case, parentObjectHandle can't be -1, and keepInPlace should be set to false)
2. parentObjectHandle: handle of the object that will become parent, or -1 if the object should become parentless. In an assembly operation, the assembly dummy on the parent object should be specified instead
3. keepInPlace: indicates whether the object's absolute pose should stay same
outputs:
replacedBy:
- name: setParent, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_setParent.method
- name: parent, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_parent.property
